# UW MarketLens — author identity canonicalization.
#
# PISAN line 67 flagged that `git shortlog -se` mixed
# `bob452305@gmail.com` across three display names. This file is
# the standard git fix: it tells log / shortlog / blame to display
# the canonical (name, email) for each contributor without
# rewriting commit history.
#
# Forward-hygiene note: this fixes the *display* of past commits.
# It doesn't prevent future misattributions. Each teammate should
# still set their identity correctly on every dev machine they
# commit from:
#
#   git config --global user.name  "<your-canonical-name>"
#   git config --global user.email "<your-canonical-email>"
#
# Going forward, new commits should land with the right (name,
# email) on the first try so this file doesn't keep growing.
#
# Format: `Canonical Name <canonical@email> Bad Name <bad@email>`
# maps the (Bad Name, bad@email) commit to the canonical pair.

# Rogagoja — primary email is rogagoja@gmail.com. The
# bob452305@gmail.com account is his too. Earlier commits using
# that account got stored with whatever `git user.name` was
# configured locally at the time — "Leonikot", lowercase
# "rogagoja", or even "dbedi06" (a Claude / tooling artifact where
# the global git name happened to be set to dbedi06 on the
# environment that committed). Email is the truth signal; all
# commits using bob452305 belong to Rogagoja.
Rogagoja <rogagoja@gmail.com> Leonikot <bob452305@gmail.com>
Rogagoja <rogagoja@gmail.com> rogagoja <bob452305@gmail.com>
Rogagoja <rogagoja@gmail.com> dbedi06 <bob452305@gmail.com>
# Catch-all for any future commit using bob452305 under a display
# name not enumerated above (e.g. a Codespace defaulting to
# "ubuntu" or "vscode"). Email-owner confirmed bob452305 is
# exclusively his, so this is safe. Git evaluates more-specific
# matches first, so the rules above still take precedence for
# named display names.
Rogagoja <rogagoja@gmail.com> <bob452305@gmail.com>

# Dilshan — his real commits use dilshanbedi@gmail.com. No
# remapping needed; line below is documentation completeness
# (`Canonical <canon@>` alone is a valid mailmap entry — leaves
# the row unchanged but signals "this is the canonical form").
dbedi06 <dilshanbedi@gmail.com>

# Lewi — canonicalize to his UW academic email so peer-review
# attribution is verifiable against @uw.edu.
Lewi <lewiale@uw.edu> Lewi <lewi@pathos.science>
